# 03 Homelab Setup

---------------------------

The goal of this experiment is to manipulate an ICMP packet and send it from a
machine running Kali Linux to a machine running Windows 11 — both connected to
the same home Wi-Fi network. This setup forms the foundation for everything that
follows.

To structure my thinking, I am going into this experiment with a set of questions
that I want to answer through hands-on work:

- How does an attacker use ICMP for his actions, and what does he accomplish by doing so?
- What Indicators of Compromise can a defender use to detect the attack?
- What defenses does the attacker have to overcome, and on which OSI layer do they operate?
- What kind of information can realistically be stolen via ICMP manipulation?
- What are the limitations of the attacker in this scenario?

These questions will guide the structure of the chapters that follow.

