## Tooling

**Scapy 2.7.01** runs on the attacker machine. It is a Python-based packet
manipulation library and serves as the primary tool for crafting and sending
custom ICMP packets throughout this experiment.

**Wireshark** is deployed on the victim machine. Capturing traffic directly
on the target system reflects the concept of host-based monitoring — it provides
the defender's perspective on the attack as it is received by the OS.

---

## Assumed Breach

This experiment does not cover initial network access. The steps required to
gain a foothold in a network involve protocols and techniques that are beyond
my knowledge. The attacker is therefore assumed to have already
gained access to the local Wi-Fi network.

Everything that happens after that point — including host discovery and target
identification — is something I will work through and document hands-on.